<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Super Group annualised yr shr up 38.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Super Group annualised yr shr up 38.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 versus previous nine months</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - fully dilted	  39.4	  vs  20.2</p>
<p>    - attrib		  39.6	  vs  21.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 11.0	  vs  nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   72.01	 vs  7.68</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   78.32	 vs  11.62</p>
<p>    Tax			 5.98	  vs  3.94</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   17.65	 vs  0.59</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,273.25    vs  285.33</p>
<p>Div payable July 23</p>
<p>on register June 13</p>
<p>Full name: Super Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said future prospects were good with various divisions operating in high growth areas. It is anticipated that the current year's earnings will show significant real growth and, once again, outperform the industrial index.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
